## Chapter 1 Introduction

The study of the structure of the nucleon-nucleon interaction in the nucleon-nucleon system has been performed by the CERN and the CERN experiments at the CERN SPS. The first results are obtained from the \(p_{T}^{2}\) collision data at \(\sqrt{s}=700\) GeV, where the \(p_{T}^{2}\) collision data were collected at \(\sqrt{s}=800\) GeV. The data were taken at \(\sqrt{s}=800\) GeV, corresponding to an integrated luminosity of \(35\times 10^{46}\) pb\({}^{-1}\).





